{"name":"Myth","hex":"#657175","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"myth","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A traditional story which embodies a belief regarding some fact or phenomenon of experience, and in which often the forces of nature and of the soul are personified; a sacred narrative regarding a god, a hero, the origin of the world or of a people, etc.","Such stories as a genre."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/myth"}],"entries":[{"title":"Myth","blocks":[{"text":"Myth is a genre of folklore consisting primarily of narratives that play a fundamental role in a society. For scholars, this is different from the ordinary sense of the term myth, meaning a belief that is not true, as the veracity of a piece of folklore is entirely irrelevant to determining whether it constitutes a myth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Hotherus_and_wood_maidens_by_Froelich.jpg/330px-Hotherus_and_wood_maidens_by_Froelich.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myth","wikidata":"Q12827256"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Francesco_Hayez_028.jpg/500px-Francesco_Hayez_028.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Francesco_Hayez_028.jpg/1280px-Francesco_Hayez_028.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Francesco_Hayez_028.jpg/500px-Francesco_Hayez_028.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Odysseus Overcome by Demodocus' Song, a mythological painting by Francesco Hayez, 1813–1815","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFrancesco_Hayez_028.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Jesus-College-MS-111_00379_190r_%28